---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="Privacy">
  <article class="reading shell">
    <h1>Privacy</h1><section>
      <h2>The userscript</h2><p>
        The userscript saves your settings and timelines in this browser's
        storage for SoundCloud. It does not upload your listening history or
        settings. Sharing a tempo link includes the settings described below.
      </p><p>
        The audio libraries, Signalsmith and Mediabunny, are included in the
        userscript download. Audio comes directly from SoundCloud. Your
        userscript manager contacts the download website to check for updates.
        SoundCloud's own privacy practices still apply.
      </p>
    </section><section>
      <h2>Shared links</h2><p>
        A shared link includes the track, duration, tempo and pitch points,
        fades and pitch mode. Anyone with the link can read those settings.
        Website share links keep them after the # in the URL, which browsers
        normally leave out of the page request. The page's scripts can still
        read them. Pressing Play sends the track link to this site's backend to
        find the audio; tempo and pitch settings stay in your browser. Opening
        the track on SoundCloud with shared settings passes them in the URL's
        query string.
      </p>
    </section><section>
      <h2>This website</h2><p>
        This website has no analytics, ads or embedded payment services. Fonts
        and screenshots load from the same website. The hosting provider may
        keep access logs.
      </p><p>
        The synth sample and audio files play locally. Chosen files are not
        uploaded. Loading a SoundCloud link sends that link to this site's
        backend and SoundCloud. The backend temporarily caches track details and
        stream links for one minute. Audio streams directly from SoundCloud to
        your browser. It is not stored by this site. Copy link writes to the
        clipboard when pressed.
      </p>
    </section><section>
      <h2>Donations</h2><p>
        Copy address only writes the displayed address to your clipboard. The
        site does not connect to a wallet or send a payment. If you donate, the
        transaction is recorded on the public blockchain for that network.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Page>
